    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "https://naccnaca-eventimages.s3.amazonaws.com/38404/shelley_and_pouliot__large.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Three things to know:\n\n\n\tComposer Jean Sibelius was so adored by his fellow Finns that his face appeared on Finland’s 100 markka banknote for decades.\n\tA coded protest against the Soviet regime, Shostakovich’s First Violin Concerto was kept hidden in a locked drawer for seven years.  \n\tJocelyn Morlock’s musical tribute to Amanda Todd searches for hope and empathy in the face of the teenager’s tragic death.\n\n\nFinnish composer Jean Sibelius described his Second Symphony as “a great river flowing to the sea,” but generations of Finns have..."
      }
